  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liberia Household Income and Expenditure Survey - Liberia Household Income Expenditure Survey</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Liberia statistisk hush&#xe5;llsunders&#xf6;kning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved capacity of the national statistics system in provision of national accounts, price and poverty data, and baseline indicators for the Agenda for Transformation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The World Bank has applied to the Embassy for funding of 4,900,000 SEK (approximately USD 600,000) to carry out the Liberia Household Income and Expenditure Survey during 2015-2016.  

The intervention aims to improve the capacity of the national statistics system in Liberia, in provision of national accounts, price and poverty data and baseline indicators for the Agenda for Transformation. The aim is set to be achieved through the completion of a 12-month Household Income and Expenditure Survey, covering seasonal variations.  

The intervention&apos;s total budget is USD 3,796,061. The other donors are USAID and the EU. The Liberian government is also funding the intervention.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">V&#xe4;rldsbanken har ans&#xf6;kt till ambassaden om finansiering p&#xe5; 4 900 000 SEK (ungef&#xe4;r 600 000 USD) f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra projektet Liberia Household Income and Expenditure Survey under 2015-2016. 

Projektet syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kapaciteten hos det nationella statistiksystemet i Liberia, i tillhandah&#xe5;llandet av nationalr&#xe4;kenskaperna, pris- och fattigdomsdata och indikatorer f&#xf6;r den liberianska fattigdomsstrategin, Agenda for Transformation. Syftet ska uppn&#xe5;s genom genomf&#xf6;randet av en 12 m&#xe5;nader l&#xe5;ng unders&#xf6;kning om hush&#xe5;llens inkomster och utgifter, som t&#xe4;cker s&#xe4;songsvariationer.

Insatsens totala budget &#xe4;r 3 796 061 USD. &#xd6;vriga givare &#xe4;r USAID och EU. &#xc4;ven den liberianska regeringen tillf&#xf6;r medel.</narrative>
  </description>
